<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Zirid emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">972 CE – 1148 CE · capital Kairouan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Sanhaja Berber dynasty that ruled Ifriqiya for the Fatimids, broke away, and was ruined by the Banu Hilal invasions.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mu'izz moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 972, he left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buluggin-ibn-ziri">Buluggin ibn Ziri</a>, son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanhaja">Sanhaja Berber</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziri-ibn-manad">Ziri ibn Manad</a>, who had served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> loyally from his fortress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashir">Ashir</a>. The Zirids ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> as hereditary governors of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zirid-dynasty">Zirid</a> rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> reached its height as a centre of trade, crafts and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maliki-school">Maliki</a> scholarship, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> exported grain, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olive-oil">olive oil</a> and textiles. In 1015 the western lands broke away under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hammadid-emirate">Hammadid emirate</a>. Around 1048 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-muizz-ibn-badis">al-Mu'izz ibn Badis</a> rejected Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiism">Shiism</a> and recognised the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, a move welcomed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> majority.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In revenge the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> encouraged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hilal">Banu Hilal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-sulaym">Banu Sulaym</a> Arab tribes to move west. They defeated the Zirids at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-haydaran">Haydaran</a> in 1052, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> was abandoned in 1057. Confined to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a> and the coast, the dynasty ended in 1148 when the Normans of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-africa">Kingdom of Africa</a> took Mahdia.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 972 CE – 1148 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.04%;width:3.50%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>972 CE – 1148 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kairouan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Buluggin ibn Ziri, al-Mu'izz ibn Badis, al-Hasan ibn Ali</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam (Ismaili), later Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, <a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a>, <a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zirids, Zirid dynasty of Ifriqiya, Zirid Ifriqiya</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1060&amp;focus